  "measures": [],
  "notes": "A plano-concave cavity, 100 mm long, with a gain sheet (a Nd:YAG rod as a thin sheet, line centre 1064 nm) inside. The flat mirror reflects 99%, the output coupler 95%. A weak seed shows the cavity’s mode. The round trip loses 6%, so the gain must make that up. Click either mirror and press Show on its cavity card: below threshold it gives the gain a pass needed (×1.031 here); above it, it says the cavity lases and by how much the round trip gains. Sweep the gain a pass to find the threshold, or change the output coupler. Gain saturation, and so the power a laser settles at, is not modelled."
